summary: It tests sudo correctness of users' groups.
description: |
    Verify that sudo correctly resolves group membership when runas_default is
    set, ensuring that running 'sudo id' does not report bogus group memberships
    such as groups=0(root).
contact: Dalibor Pospíšil <dapospis@redhat.com>
test: ./runtest.sh
recommend:
- sudo
duration: 10m
enabled: true
tag:
- CI-Tier-1
- SP-TBU
- TIPpass_Security
- Tier1
- Tier1security
- fedora-wanted
- rhel9-wanted
tier: '1'
extra-summary: /CoreOS/sudo/Regression/bz497873-sudo-gives-bogus-group-membership-if-runas_default-is-used
extra-task: /CoreOS/sudo/Regression/bz497873-sudo-gives-bogus-group-membership-if-runas_default-is-used
